## Problem classes

### `Nearby Connections fights the hotspot`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Hotspot or Wi-Fi Direct drops as soon as the invite connects | Nearby Connections upgrades its own link onto Wi-Fi | Keep control traffic on Bluetooth or GATT. Do not add the Nearby Connections SDK. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Third phone starts a second network`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A joiner tap creates a new hotspot | Advert lacked role and group id, or the client ignored them | Advert includes role, group id, and host id. A phone already in a group invites into that group. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Password prompt abort drops the transfer`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| User dismisses the PSK field and the peer disappears | Skip was treated as Decline | Missing PSK falls through to the host chain. Only short-code decline and link-sheet cancel abort. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Wi-Fi Direct step kept for a non-Android joiner`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Host chain includes WFD when a desktop or iOS device must join | Host methods listed without checking every non-host | Skip `wifiDirect` when any non-host cannot join WFD (`kind != android`). Host-method lists alone are not enough |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Waiting invite dies right after the active one`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Second invite times out on the next orchestrator tick after a long first dialog | Timeout is measured from `enqueuedAt`, not promote time | On promote, reset the clock for the new active invite, or tick only against activate time. Do not change the pure queue without re-planning T02 |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->
